 "t": "The targeted agents below daraxonrasib and olaparib rest on pancreatic subsets of 21 to 38 patients, and two of them had no efficacy threshold they could have failed.",
 "why": "The sotorasib pancreatic cohort pooled 38 patients across phase 1 dose exploration, phase 1 expansion and phase 2, with <b>no prespecified response benchmark and no hypothesis test</b>, and its response interval (10% to 37%) is compatible with the under-10% historical benchmark the authors invoke. Adagrasib's prespecified 10% null applies to the pooled tumour-agnostic cohort of 57 evaluable patients, not to its 21 pancreatic patients, and six patients counted as evaluable by investigators were removed by central review for having no measurable disease, moving the denominator favourably. Zenocutuzumab's 36 pancreatic patients were <b>all KRAS wild-type</b>, its primary endpoint was investigator-assessed response with blinded central review only secondary, its primary efficacy population is a post-enrolment construct (204 treated to 158 evaluable, with short-follow-up exclusions falling on early progressors), and no progression-free or overall survival is reported for the pancreatic subgroup at all. None of the three reports a screening denominator, so the testing burden implied by any of them is invisible. The NTRK, RET, BRAF and FGFR entries were not retrieved for this depot."
