 "t": "The targeted agents below daraxonrasib and olaparib rest on pancreatic subsets of 21 to 38 patients, and two of them had no efficacy threshold they could have failed.",
 "why": "The sotorasib pancreatic cohort pooled 38 patients across phase 1 dose exploration, phase 1 expansion and phase 2, with <b>no prespecified response benchmark and no hypothesis test</b>, and its response interval (10% to 37%) is compatible with the under-10% historical benchmark the authors invoke. Adagrasib's prespecified 10% null applies to the pooled tumour-agnostic cohort of 57 evaluable patients, not to its 21 pancreatic patients, and six patients counted as evaluable by investigators were removed by central review for having no measurable disease, moving the denominator favourably. Zenocutuzumab's prespecified pancreatic cohort included 36 KRAS wild-type patients and had median PFS 9.2 months (95% CI 5.5–11.2); pancreatic OS was not reported. The trial treated 204 patients, of whom 161 met the primary-efficacy definition and 158 had measurable disease for investigator response assessment. The first-dose timing cutoff and other exclusions do not establish disproportionate exclusion of early progressors. Response and PFS estimates from this single-arm study do not establish comparative benefit. None of the three reports a screening denominator, so the testing burden implied by any of them is invisible. The NTRK, RET, BRAF and FGFR entries were not retrieved for this depot."
